Instructions to Connect to Reach Alpha 5 via Terminal
by Nolan Allen
14 January 2025

Open a terminal and run the following:
  source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
  cd ~/arm_hooking
  colcon build
  source ./install/local_setup.bash

Open subsequent terminals with the following:
  source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
  cd ~/arm_hooking
  source ./install/local_setup.bash

Next use the following commands to run the various programs:
  python3 src/tools/camera_recorder.py
  python3 src/tools/visualize_traj.py
  python3 src/tools/clean_workspace.py
  python3 src/tools/reset_arm_pos.py --serial_port /dev/ttyUSB0
  ros2 launch {package} {launch_file} {param_name}:={param_value}
  rviz2

Launch Files [parameters]
arm_control
  gamepad_keyboard_control.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size]
  arm_controller.launch.py [master_arm_serial_port, serial_port, apriltag_size]
visualization
  apriltag_pose.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size]
  focus_detection.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size, record_output, focus_threshold]
  visualize_trajectory.launch.py [generator, serial_port, apriltag_size]
record_skill
  perform_skill.launch.py [generator, serial_port, apriltag_size]
  record_skill.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size]
trajectory_generation
  generate_skill_csv.launch.py [generator, serial_port, apriltag_size]
ra_core
  reach_alpha_starter.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size]
  get_brov_cam_pose.launch.py [serial_port, apriltag_size]


The following terminal command displays the camera feed with little latency:
  gst-launch-1.0 rtspsrc location=rtsp://admin:@192.168.2.10:554/stream=1 latency=0 ! rtph264depay ! h264parse ! avdec_h264 ! videoconvert ! autovideosink
